<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-863] Potential resource leak with unclosed LedgerManager in BookieShell</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-863</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There&apos;re more than one occurrence.&lt;br/&gt;
Here is an example in ListLedgersCmd#runCmd():&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;                LedgerManagerFactory mFactory = LedgerManagerFactory.newLedgerManagerFactory(bkConf, zk);
                LedgerManager m = mFactory.newLedgerManager();
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;m is not closed upon leaving the method.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
